dynrec: add SPARC V9 64-bit backend

Derived from the PowerPC backends. Generated code runs in its own
register window, helpers are called relative to the cpu_regs base
register as the code cache is mapped out of call range of the binary.
Values passed to C functions are zero-extended as required by the ABI.
Blocks return directly with ret/restore, and on CPUs with a coherent
I-cache (UltraSPARC III and later) a single flush per block is issued.

Performance on a Sun UltraSPARC IIIi (sun4u, 1 CPU), DOSBox cycles=max,
machine=svga_s3, SB Pro, measured under Xvfb:

  Test                    normal core   dynamic core   speedup
  3DBENCH                 18.1 fps      32.2 fps       1.78x
  Doom -timedemo demo3     7.5 fps      17.7 fps       2.37x
                          (10012 rt)    (4227 rt, 2134 gametics)
  Quake +timedemo demo1    2.3 fps       5.8 fps       2.50x
                          (418.0 s)     (166.9 s, 969 frames)

Signed-off-by: René Rebe <rene@exactco.de>

